task: intent-fitted-model-ships
agent: opus5-intent
started: 2026-09-04
branch: feature/intent-fitted-model-ships
worktree: ../okay-wt-model

why: Nothing ships a fitted model and there is no documented path from
  "I have messages" to "I have a model". Every tier above the pattern
  cues needs a Trained that exists only inside a test. `Fitted` can
  write one as data and nothing writes it.

plan: CharGrams needs no embedder at all, so it is the tier that CAN
  ship — fit it on the fixture, serialise with Fitted, commit the
  artifact, and load it with no network and no fitting on the startup
  path. Measure dim against size and accuracy before choosing. Plus
  the door a caller uses for their OWN data, and a test that the
  shipped artifact reproduces from the same corpus, so it is not a
  mystery blob.

honesty: it is a worked example fitted on ~150 author-written
  messages over four meeting classes, not a general intent model, and
  the doc must say so with the held-out number beside it.

files: okay-intent/src/main/scala/okay/intent/{Models,Fit}.scala,
  the artifact, okay-intent tests, docs/modules/okay-intent.md,
  specs/intent-classify.md, BACKLOG.md
